WEBVTT

00:00:28.663 --> 00:00:30.204
So why is it important?

00:00:30.204 --> 00:00:32.621
Of course you probably know the answer.

00:00:32.621 --> 00:00:35.162
One hundred dollar bill
is printed by the Government

00:00:35.162 --> 00:00:36.996
and designated as official currency,

00:00:36.996 --> 00:00:39.454
while the other pieces of paper are not.

00:00:39.454 --> 00:00:41.829
But it just makes them legal.

00:00:41.829 --> 00:00:45.037
On the other hand, what gives its value
to a hundred dollar bill,

00:00:45.037 --> 00:00:48.621
is the number, more or less important,
of these banknotes in circulation.

00:00:48.621 --> 00:00:52.412
Throughout history, most currencies,
the US dollar including

00:00:52.412 --> 00:00:54.246
were linked to the value of the goods

00:00:54.246 --> 00:00:57.537
and their quantity in circulation
was determined according to reserves

00:00:57.537 --> 00:00:59.287
of gold or silver from a government.

00:00:59.287 --> 00:01:02.579
But after the United States has
abolished this system in 1971,